From 5252a7d0a960dcf1ea2620357a51bee2d207a993 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andreas Baierl <ichgeh@imkreisrum.de>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 18:06:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 184/267] fixup! media: amlogic: amvdec: add H.264 decoding

media: amlogic: amvdec: h264: abort on an unexpected status of a frame

The threaded interrupt handler aborts on an unexpected firmware status
only for field pictures. For frame pictures the status is ignored, but
the firmware waits for an action, so the job never finishes and the
decoder hangs until userspace stops the queues.

This happens with a damaged access unit, e.g. with lost slices after a
reception error: the firmware runs out of input before the picture is
complete and reports SEARCH_BUFEMPTY (0x22). The whole access unit is
fed at once, so no more input arrives for the picture.

Abort on an unexpected status of frame pictures too, like HEVC and VP9
do for any status they don't handle.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Andreas Baierl <ichgeh@imkreisrum.de>
Signed-off-by: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/amlogic/amvdec/codec_h264.c | 12 +++++++++---
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/amlogic/amvdec/codec_h264.c b/drivers/media/platform/amlogic/amvdec/codec_h264.c
index f96e5c7dc966..62321b6506e7 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/amlogic/amvdec/codec_h264.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/amlogic/amvdec/codec_h264.c
@@ -1908,9 +1908,15 @@ static irqreturn_t codec_h264_threaded_isr(struct amvdec_session *sess)
 				h264->multi_done_pending = true;
 				schedule_work(&sess->esparser_queue_work);
 			}
-		} else if (h264->multi_field_picture) {
-			dev_err_ratelimited(core->dev_dec, "h264 field: unexpected status=%#x phase=%u\n",
-					    status, READ_ONCE(h264->multi_field_phase));
+		} else {
+			/*
+			 * Any other status (e.g. the firmware ran out of input on a
+			 * damaged access unit) waits for an action, which isn't sent.
+			 * Abort, otherwise the job never finishes.
+			 */
+			dev_err_ratelimited(core->dev_dec, "h264 multi: unexpected status=%#x field=%u phase=%u\n",
+					    status, h264->multi_field_picture,
+					    READ_ONCE(h264->multi_field_phase));
 			codec_h264_multi_abort(sess);
 		}
 		return IRQ_HANDLED;
